n by the approuter. This is done by setting the CEP.EnableCsrfProtection property to true for all dynamic destinations where their respective backend doesn’t handle CSRF protection.  If your backend is already protected, there’s no need to add this\",458\n28,\"8 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: CSRF Protection for Dynamic Destinations\nDescription: Today our approuters do not provide CSRF protection for dynamic destinations. It’s assumed that backends behind the destinations, handle CSRF protection on their own.   New security measures have been introduced to enable CSRF protection by the approuter. This is done by setting the CEP.EnableCsrfProtection property to true for all dynamic destinations where their respective backend doesn’t handle CSRF protection.  If your backend is already protected, there’s no need to add this property. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3119 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 1.93.0\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 1 has been updated from version 1.92.0 to 1.93.0. Updated components:      Apache Tomcat 9 is updated from version 9.0.86 to 9.0.87      Apache TomEE 7 is updated from version 7.0.9.sap-41 to 7.0.9.sap-42      PostgreSQL JDBC Driver (postgresql.version) is updated from 42.7.2 to 42.7.3      SAP HANA Driver (hana.driver.2.X.X) is updated from version 2.19.16 to 2.20.11    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-08\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3120 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 2.6.0\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 2 has been updated from version 2.4.0 to 2.5.0. Updated components:      Apache Tomcat 10 is updated from version 10.1.19 to 10.1.20      PostgreSQL JDBC Driver (postgresql.version) is updated from 42.7.2 to 42.7.3      SAP HANA Driver (hana.driver.2.X.X) is updated from version 2.19.16 to 2.20.11    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-08\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n\",320\n27,\"--- Record 3111 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Public Workspace: Access for Non-Member External Users.\nDescription: External users who are not workspace members are unable to search for a workspace or see content uploaded by members. However, when adding a specific external user to the Access Policy user list, that user can explore and find this workspace, be invited to the workspace, be mentioned in chats, and see content uploaded by the workspace members.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3112 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Removal of External Workspace Type\nDescription:   It's no longer possible to create an external workspace. When you create a new workspace, you can choose between creating a public workspace or a private workspace.  Existing external workspaces will become private workspaces and an External warning icon will be added to the workspace header to indicate that the content of this workspace is visible to external users.  You can invite external users to both private and public workspaces. To do that, when you create a new workspace (or when you edit the admin settings of an existing workspace), you need to choose the option \"\"External users can access this workspace and be invited as members\"\". Note that the invited external users should already be added to the system prior to the invitation. For more information about external users, seeAbout External Users  If the workspace setting \"\"Allow users to request to join this workspace\"\" is enabled, users can request to join this workspace by going to Workspaces  View All Workspaces   Explore Workspaces and clicking Join Workspace next to the workspace name. Alternatively, they can open the workspace and click the Join button at the top right.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-14\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3113 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Role-Based Filtering of Cards\nDescription: With the transition to the Content Manager as the card management tool, all cards will be assigned to roles and will be accessible at runtime based on user roles.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3114 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support Custom SMTP Configuration\nDescription: Customers can choose to use their own SMTP server settings instead of the default settings. To configure the SMTP settings, go to Admin Console, External Integration  SMTP Configuration and add the custom SMTP settings. To go back to the default SMTP settings, simply delete the custom configuration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3115 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support of Cards as App Visualization Type\nDescription:   Cards are now supported as a visualization type of local apps and are maintained in the Content Manager - App editor – Visualization tab.  It is no longer possible to manually upload standalone cards or update cards through the Admin Console. Remaining functionality in the Admin Console is configuring the card and enabling/disabling the card.   It is no longer possible to directly deploy a card created via the Development Tools for SAP Build Work Zone extension in SAP Business Application Studio to the subaccount.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3116 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support of Custom Domains in Private Networks\nDescription: To support the use of a custom domain resolvable only in customer’s own private networks, customers should open a support ticket on component EP-WZ-DMN to request this. Further instructions will be provided by the support team.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3117 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: System Info on the Overview Page\nDescription: The Overview page of a workspace has been enhanced with additional information that can be added to support tickets.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3118 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: CSRF Protection for Dynamic Destinations\nDescription: Today our approuters do not provide CSRF protection for dynamic destinations. It’s assumed that backends behind the destinations, handle CSRF protection on their own.   New security measures have been introduced to enable CSRF protection by the approuter. This is done by setting the CEP.EnableCsrfProtection property to true for all dynamic destinations where their respective backend doesn\",320\n277,\" CSRF Protection for Dynamic Destinations\nDescription: Today our approuters do not provide CSRF protection for dynamic destinations. It’s assumed that backends behind the destinations, handle CSRF protection on their own.   New security measures have been introduced to enable CSRF protection by the approuter. This is done by setting the CEP.EnableCsrfProtection property to true for all dynamic destinations where their respective backend doesn’t handle CSRF protection.  If your backend is already protected, there’s no need to add this property. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3110 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Exporting Workspaces with Images\nDescription: The following issue has been fixed: when exporting a workspace that contains workpages with embedded images, those workpages will be lost when the workspace is imported. This issue has been fixed and all embedded images can be found under /content/workpage_xxx/images/.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n\",320\n\n\nOutput:\n", "role": "user"}], "parameters": {"model": "unsloth/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct", "frequency_penalty": 0.0, "max_tokens": null, "n": 1, "presence_penalty": 0.0, "temperature": 0.0, "top_p": 1.0, "response_format": {"type": "json_object"}}}, "key": "chat_create_community_report_9cab64fb5298c55031de786d1aeaf2fc37ef57666e6dc8be69951eded0950e69_v2"}